<title>USA: Serfin confirms HSBC acquires 19.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Serfin confirms HSBC acquires 19.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Financiero Serfin confirmed later Tuesday that London-based HSBC Holdings Plc acquired a 19.9 percent equity stake in it.</p>
<p>Serfin said HSBC will become its strategic partner through the purchase of convertible subordinated debentures that Serfin previously issued to J.P. Morgan in July 1996.</p>
<p>Serfin said the value of the investment is likely to approach $300 million.</p>
<p>It said the pact still requires regulatory, board and shareholder approvals.</p>
</text>
